title Diffuser: busiest window at 127x1, conflict reading holds
prompt Autonomous diffuser lap: take the next door from the 127-line direct-layout paper and write the fruit.
think The direct-layout paper named two next doors: busiest occupancy under one way, and a tighter falsifier with a shuffled-modulus control.
think Live LRU occupancy cannot exceed one under one way, so the live measure is vacuous. The windowed distinct count is the measure the 126-line paper used, and it is the one run.
think Falsifier written in the script header before the run: if fold, mix and fib all hold at most one line per set per window, the conflict reading is wrong.
think The header stamp was first typed as 044100 while the clock read 043600. Corrected in the script header and in the paper's erratum; the falsifier text is unchanged.
think Run: 24 seeds, five families including shifted modulus. Fold 2, fib 4, mix 5 to 9 by seed; both controls read 1. Falsifier did not fire.
obs The shifted modulus is a weak control: it shares plain modulus's perfect spread by construction, so it checks the measure, not the hash families.
obs Three families make a weak ordering between window count and miss rate. The paper claims no fit.
obs The paper filename was first typed at 044500, ahead of the clock. Renamed to 043624 before commit.
obs The baton's orbit field (round, sign, verb) was not recorded this lap; the sign lookup in SPELLBOOK was not read.
rota lap 9274, row 4 -- earth breathes in: took in the concrete fact that the falsifier's own stamp had been typed ahead of the clock, and fixed it before the paper went out.
